# Mini App UI

- One simple mobile-friendly page; two stacked sections (create shares / recover).
- No framework, tabs, card grids, animations, settings dialogs, or Copy All.
- Use the exact DOM IDs listed in `AGENTS.md` section 7.
- Dangerous copy actions need the brief's warning text; clipboard write only on explicit button handlers.
- Never call `navigator.clipboard.readText()` in app code.
- Required visible hackathon / disposable-wallet warnings must remain.
- Telegram WebView realities (see `docs/telegram-launcher-notes.md`): opens full-screen height, runs on Android/iOS/Desktop, must load fast (tiny bundle, no fonts/frameworks), must not overflow at narrow widths.
- Render identically with or without `tgWebApp*` query params — ignore them all; no Telegram SDK (`telegram-web-app.js`, `@telegram-apps/*`, `@twa-dev/*`).
